{
  "name": "multi-site-vulns",
  "integration": "claroty-ctd",
  "description": "REGRESSION LOCK on cross-site CVE mis-attribution. An EMC aggregates several CTDs and the bare numeric asset id is site-scoped -- that is the whole reason resource_id embeds site_id -- so asset 30 exists at BOTH site 1 and site 2. The vulnerability endpoint's asset_id column carries the numeric id in some deployments and the resource id in others. Trying both spellings at lookup credited BOTH assets with the same finding: site 2's PLC was given a vulnerability belonging only to site 1. Rows are now canonicalised to the resource-id form at index time using the row's own site_id, and a row carrying no site at all is claimed by the first matching asset and then removed, so the join can be lossy but never wrong. Row A names 30-2 explicitly, row B names 30 with site_id 1, row C names 31 with no site at all. Each asset must end with exactly one finding.",
